From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: debugfs-client: allow writes for s2idle testing

The Odin 3 s2idle hang goes away when the APPS sleep set keeps a DDR
vote (the PCIe suspend OPP floor) and comes back with any AOSS-level
DDR or sleep restriction, so the next step is to find which BCM vote in
the sleep set matters. The debugfs test client can place arbitrary
votes with a tag (QCOM_ICC_TAG_SLEEP for sleep-only) but its write side
is compiled out. Enable it for testing only.
---
--- a/drivers/interconnect/debugfs-client.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/debugfs-client.c
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
  * configuration option for this feature.
  * People who want to use this will need to modify the source code directly.
  */
-#undef INTERCONNECT_ALLOW_WRITE_DEBUGFS
+#define INTERCONNECT_ALLOW_WRITE_DEBUGFS
 
 #if defined(INTERCONNECT_ALLOW_WRITE_DEBUGFS) && defined(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS)
 
